    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "One function, three orders",
     "say": "Here's the whole algorithm. A node holds a value, a left child, and a right child. If the node is empty, stop: that's the base case. Walk the left subtree. Print the node. Walk the right subtree. On our tree it prints one, three, six, eight, ten, fourteen. Move the print above both calls and you get preorder. Move it below both and you get postorder.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "void walk(Node* n) {\n    if (!n) return;\n    walk(n->left);\n    cout << n->val << ' ';\n    walk(n->right);\n}"
      }
     ],
